{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"983","artifact_type":"feature-context","name":"plan/feature-context-subdirectory-namespace-warning.md@sha256:19ed5028021a4686ad2be03ca8ee60fb25f0308315c2af51b2e0d4eef0dc0612"},"owner_reference":"983","content":"# ARTIFACT:DISCOVERY\n\n## Feature\n\nDocument the \"skills/agents in subdirectories silently fail to register\" warning in the two plugin-creator reference skills that plugin authors and audit agents actually consult.\n\n## Problem Statement\n\n`.claude/rules/markdown-file-references.md` (previously `.claude/CLAUDE.md` lines 411\u2013418, added in commit `ea33cf2e`) states the canonical rule: skill directories nested under `skills/` (e.g. `skills/testing/foo/SKILL.md`) silently fail to register \u2014 Claude Code only auto-discovers skills one level deep under `skills/`. Subdirectory colon-namespacing (`plugin:group:skill`) is a `commands/` feature only, not a `skills/`/`agents/` feature.\n\nThis warning was added only to the project-level rule file. It was never propagated to the two AI-facing reference skills that plugin authors and audit agents load when reasoning about plugin/skill structure: `plugin-creator:claude-plugins-reference-2026` and `plugin-creator:claude-skills-overview-2026`. Verified via grep (2026-08-16): neither file contains the warning \u2014 `claude-plugins-reference-2026/SKILL.md` has zero matches for \"subdirectory\"; `claude-skills-overview-2026/SKILL.md`'s only \"subdirectory\" match is an unrelated `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}` description, not this warning.\n\nConsequence observed in the field: the `doc-drift-auditor` agent reported 10 phantom skills because it expected `skills/workflows/discovery/SKILL.md`-style nesting to register \u2014 it does not. Any agent or human author relying on these two reference skills (not the project rule file, which is scoped to this repo only) will repeat the same mistake.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. `plugin-creator:claude-plugins-reference-2026/SKILL.md` contains a warning section stating that skill/agent directories nested under `skills/`/`agents/` silently fail to register.\n2. `plugin-creator:claude-skills-overview-2026/SKILL.md` contains an equivalent warning with a concrete wrong/right example.\n3. Warning wording in both files states the same constraint as the canonical rule in `.claude/rules/markdown-file-references.md` (\"Subdirectory Namespaces \u2014 Skills Do NOT Support This\" section) \u2014 same substance, adapted to each file's existing voice/structure.\n4. `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` and `README.md` invocation paths confirmed flat (no `dh:group:skill`-style paths) \u2014 verified 2026-08-16 via grep, already correct, no edit needed.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n\n1. Do not re-litigate or restate the original (incorrect) premise that subdirectory namespacing is a supported `skills/` feature \u2014 the RT-ICA assessment already corrected this; the deliverable is a warning against the pattern, not a how-to for using it.\n2. Do not modify `commands/` documentation \u2014 namespacing IS a real `commands/` feature and is out of scope here.\n3. Do not touch other plugins' reference skills beyond the two named files unless a broader grep during planning turns up additional undocumented copies of the same gap.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n1. Both target skill files contain an explicit, unambiguous statement: skill/agent directories one level deeper than `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` or `agents/<name>.md` are not discovered by Claude Code.\n2. `claude-skills-overview-2026` includes a wrong/right example pair (e.g. `skills/testing/foo/SKILL.md` \u2192 silently dead vs. `skills/foo/SKILL.md` \u2192 `/plugin:foo` \u2192 correct).\n3. `claude-plugins-reference-2026` includes an equivalent \"Subdirectory Warning\" section appropriate to its content (plugin schema / auto-discovery documentation).\n\n### Non-Functional\n\n1. Wording must not contradict the canonical rule file \u2014 any future edit to the canonical rule should be trivially diffable against these two copies.\n2. Markdown lint (`markdownlint-cli2`) and `skilllint` must pass on the modified files (existing CI gates `lint-markdown`, `validate-plugins`).\n\n## Design Questions for Planning\n\n1. The backlog item's own \"Files to update\" list also named `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` and `README.md` \u2014 verified during discovery (2026-08-16 grep) these already have zero colon-namespaced invocation paths, so no edit is needed there. Planning should confirm this with its own check before finalizing task scope, but should not add a task to edit files that are already correct.\n2. Exact placement/section-heading style in each target skill is a planning/architecture decision (match each skill's existing structure) \u2014 not prescribed here.\n\n## References\n\n- `.claude/rules/markdown-file-references.md` \u2014 canonical rule, section \"Subdirectory Namespaces \u2014 Skills Do NOT Support This\"\n- Commit `ea33cf2e` \u2014 \"docs(CLAUDE): document subdirectory namespace convention for skills and agents\" (added the canonical rule, scope: `.claude/CLAUDE.md` only)\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-plugins-reference-2026/SKILL.md` \u2014 target file 1\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-skills-overview-2026/SKILL.md` \u2014 target file 2\n- Backlog item #983 body \u2014 original Groomed (2026-04-15) section, Acceptance Criteria, RT-ICA Assessment (APPROVED-WITH-CORRECTION-TO-PREMISE)\n\n## Resolved Questions\n\n| Question | Answer | Source |\n|----------|--------|--------|\n| Is subdirectory namespacing actually supported for skills? | No \u2014 silently fails to register; only `commands/` supports colon namespacing | `.claude/rules/markdown-file-references.md`, confirmed by RT-ICA premise correction on the item |\n| Has this warning already been added anywhere? | Yes, only to `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (now `.claude/rules/markdown-file-references.md`) via commit `ea33cf2e` \u2014 not to the two target reference skills | `git log --grep`, direct grep of both target files (2026-08-16) |\n| Are the dh CLAUDE.md/README.md invocation paths already flat? | Yes \u2014 grep for `/dh:[a-z0-9-]+:[a-z0-9-]+` returns zero matches in both files | Direct grep (2026-08-16) |\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone \u2014 no unbound constraints, domain knowledge gaps, or contradictory requirements identified.\n\n## User Confirmation\n\n- [x] AUTO_MODE \u2014 treated as confirmed. Discovery derived entirely from the backlog item's existing Groomed/RT-ICA content plus direct verification against current repo state (git log, grep) rather than fresh interactive Q&A.\n"}